  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "+ofpbIy3bNkTn9W4Y5pkl3gpqkc=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:34:48.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The entire GraphQL surface of the Analytics Engine is one field:\n\n```graphql\ntype AnalyticsQuery {\n  series(filter: AnalyticsFilter): [AnalyticsPeriod]\n}\n\nextend type Query {\n  analytics: AnalyticsQuery\n}\n```\n\nNo mutations are declared anywhere in the schema, and the docs state it plainly: data cannot be input through GraphQL. Writes go through `IAnalyticsStore` in TypeScript, from a processor or a script. Treat the GraphQL layer as strictly a reporting surface.\n\n`AnalyticsFilter` must be **fully populated** \u2014 it is not a partial where the engine fills in defaults. All six of `start`, `end`, `granularity`, `metrics`, `dimensions` (each with `name`, `select`, `lod`), and `currency` are required for the query to function. The characteristic symptom of a partial filter is not a validation message but a bare `\"Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'filter')\"`.\n\nCase sensitivity is the other common failure. Metric names and granularity values are matched exactly, so `Monthlyu` produces an enum error suggesting `monthly`, and a mistyped metric produces an error listing the valid names.\n\nA useful exploration technique from the best-practices page: start with a broad `select` and a high `lod` (e.g. `select: \"atlas\"`, `lod: 5`) to *discover* which sub-paths exist under a dimension, then narrow the `select` path once you know the hierarchy. The high-lod response is effectively a directory listing of the dimension tree.\n\nProvenance: drafts `03-Build/04-WorkWithData/_06-Analytics Engine/graphql/index.md` and `.../best-practices.md`; schema verified in `packages/analytics-engine/graphql/src/schema.ts` (zero occurrences of `Mutation`) and the read-only statement in `.../_06-Analytics Engine/intro.md`, at 6.2.2-dev.45.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:34:48.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:34:48.000Z"
    }
  },
